    "notes": "MeshWX v5 (spec 5.0). Every message is the data field of one MeshCore GRP_DATA packet on #meshwx with data_type 0xFF10, at most 165 bytes. All multi-byte integers are little-endian; times are Unix minutes as u32. The type byte is (type << 4) | flags. Warnings are keyed by (event, office, etn), not by seq. Coverage (type 8, spec 7A) is the bot's own statement of what it carries: centre, radius in km, office indices, and its zones as the same UGC runs a warning's area list uses; a set flag means that list was cut, so a code missing from it means 'not stated', never 'not covered'. Never infer a bot's coverage from the stations or warnings you happen to have received. Indices into offices/stations/states come from index.json; event codes from 'events' and sky codes from 'sky_codes' in this file. The v3/v4 keys above are retained for legacy clients and are unrelated to v5."
